<title>UK: MAM lowers stake in Imperial Tobacco.</title>
<headline>MAM lowers stake in Imperial Tobacco.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>British fund management giant Mercury Asset Management Group Plc (MAM) has reduced its holding in Imperial Tobacco Group to below 10 percent, the level at which stakes must be notified, the tobacco firm said on Friday.</p>
<p>Imperial Tobacco said it had been notified by MAM that the fund manager's holding had fallen from the 10.96 percent it announced on May 22. This level was in itself a decrease from MAM's 11.11 percent holding on May 12.</p>
<p>The company did not say what MAM's stake now was.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
